{
  "info": {
    "name": "Guild Service (Team 14)",
    "description": "Guild identity, membership, roles and real-time guild chat.\n\nOwner: IsStephy. Default port: 8087.\n\nEvery request goes through the gateway in the shared stack: the gateway verifies the player's token, drops it, and forwards `X-Gateway-Key` (proving the request came through it) plus `X-User-Id` (the player). This service never verifies tokens and answers 401 to anything without a valid `X-Gateway-Key`, except /health and /docs.\n\nThis collection talks to the service directly, so it sends those two headers itself - it plays the gateway. Set the `gatewayKey` variable to the GATEWAY_KEY in your .env (the default, `change_me`, matches .env.example). To go through the real gateway with real logins, use collections/gateway.postman_collection.json.\n\nGuild roles are checked by this service against its own data. `GET /guilds/{guildId}` also accepts Monster Raid's `X-Service-Key` instead of a player (set `monsterRaidServiceKey` to SERVICE_KEY_MONSTER_RAID).\n\nRun the requests top to bottom: `Create Guild` saves the new guildId, so every later request works without copy-pasting anything.\n\nThe WebSocket chat endpoint cannot be stored in Postman's collection file format; see the `Guild Chat (WebSocket)` folder for how to open it in the app.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:8087"
    },
    {
      "key": "guildId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "ownerId",
      "value": "u-owner-1"
    },
    {
      "key": "memberId",
      "value": "u-member-2"
    },
    {
      "key": "inviteeId",
      "value": "u-member-3"
    },
    {
      "key": "unknownUserId",
      "value": "unknown-user-99"
    },
    {
      "key": "gatewayKey",
      "value": "change_me"
    },
    {
      "key": "monsterRaidServiceKey",
      "value": "change_me"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Health",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/health",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "health"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Liveness check. Returns { status: ok, service: guild-service }."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "Create Guild",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('201 Created', function () { pm.response.to.have.status(201); });",
              "const body = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test('returns guildId and name', function () {",
              "    pm.expect(body).to.have.property('guildId');",
              "    pm.expect(body).to.have.property('name');",
              "});",
              "// Save the id so the rest of the collection can use it.",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('guildId', body.guildId);",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('guildName', body.name);"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "X-Gateway-Key",
            "value": "{{gatewayKey}}"
          },
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          },
          {
            "key": "X-User-Id",
            "value": "{{ownerId}}"
          }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Night Owls {{$timestamp}}\",\n  \"ownerId\": \"{{ownerId}}\"\n}"
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/guilds",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "guilds"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Creates a new guild. The ownerId becomes the guild's first member with role `owner`.\n\nIdentity is verified against User Management Service (mocked in Lab 1) - an unknown ownerId returns 404."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "Search Guilds",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('200 OK', function () { pm.response.to.have.status(200); });",
              "pm.test('returns an array', function () { pm.expect(pm.response.json()).to.be.an('array'); });"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "X-Gateway-Key",
            "value": "{{gatewayKey}}"
          },
          {
            "key": "X-User-Id",
            "value": "{{ownerId}}"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/guilds/search?query=night&limit=10&offset=0",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "guilds",
            "search"
          ],
          "query": [
            {
              "key": "query",
              "value": "night",
              "description": "Case-insensitive substring of the guild name."
            },
            {
              "key": "limit",
              "value": "10",
              "description": "Page size, integer 1-100. Defaults to 20."
            },
            {
              "key": "offset",
              "value": "0",
              "description": "Rows to skip, integer >= 0. Defaults to 0."
            }
          ]
        },
        "description": "Searches guilds by name. Each result carries the guild's current memberCount."
      },
      "response": []
    },
