    {
      "name": "Guild Chat (WebSocket)",
      "description": "`WS /guilds/{guildId}/chat` - real-time guild chat.\n\nPostman's collection file format (v2.1) cannot store WebSocket requests, so open it inside the Postman app.\n\nThe socket needs a single-use ticket from the gateway - the chat checks it instead of a user token:\n\n1. Through the gateway, as a logged-in player (see collections/gateway.postman_collection.json):\n   GET http://localhost:8080/ws/negotiate?path=/guilds/<guildId>/chat\n   Authorization: Bearer <token>\n   -> { \"wsUrl\": \"ws://localhost:8087/guilds/<guildId>/chat?ticket=<ticket>\" }\n2. New -> WebSocket Request, URL: the wsUrl from step 1. Connect within 60 seconds - the ticket expires, and opens one socket only.\n3. The server immediately sends the existing history:\n   { \"type\": \"history\", \"messages\": [] }\n4. Send this JSON message, with authorId = the player you logged in as:\n   { \"authorId\": \"<your userId>\", \"message\": \"hello guild\" }\n5. The server stamps it and broadcasts it to every connected member:\n   { \"authorId\": \"<your userId>\", \"message\": \"hello guild\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-06T12:11:03.692Z\" }\n\nRules: a missing, expired, reused or wrong-path ticket, an unknown guild, or a caller who is not a member closes the socket with 1008; too many open sockets close it with 1013. authorId must be the ticket's player.\n\nTo demonstrate the broadcast, negotiate twice (one ticket per socket) and send from one of the two tabs.",
      "item": []
    }
  ],
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "prerequest",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// Guard against running a request before the one that sets its variable.",
          "const url = pm.request.url.toString();",
          "const headers = JSON.stringify(pm.request.headers);",
          "const needed = [",
          "    { name: 'guildId', setBy: 'Create Guild' },",
          "];",
          "",
          "needed.forEach(function (v) {",
          "    const token = '{{' + v.name + '}}';",
          "    if (url.indexOf(token) === -1 && headers.indexOf(token) === -1) return;",
          "    if (!pm.collectionVariables.get(v.name)) {",
          "        throw new Error(",
          "            'Collection variable {{' + v.name + '}} is empty. Run \"' + v.setBy +",
          "            '\" first, or use Run Collection so the requests execute in order.'",
          "        );",
          "    }",
          "});"
        ]
      }
    }
  ]
}
